-- lib/derive.cub — generic programming over the data table (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”, its part F31: deriving as terms
-- over %dent producing codes). Loaded after lib/check.cub. derive-eq d: the code of a decidable
-- equality on the data type d, read off its constructors' telescopes: a word field compares by
-- %weq, a recursive field by the hypothesis the case provides, a field of another data type by that
-- type's derived equality; constructors with dimensions (higher inductive types) and other field
-- types are not covered (none). The code evaluates (eval-g) and quotes like any other.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- shapes
--
-- the kinds of a constructor's fields, by walking its telescope with fresh variables: a Lst of
-- (kind , d2): kind 0 a word, 1 recursive, 2 a data type d2 without parameters; none otherwise
-- (some kinds, or none)
dfield-kind d A =
  if is-rec-ty d A then some (#1 , d)
  else (case A of
          tword → some (#0 , d)
          tdata d2 ps V → (case ps of lnil → some (#2 , d2); _ → none)
          tg g nm → (case %view (%gval g) of wpty k n → (if %weq k #4 then none else some (#3 , k)); _ → none)
          _ → none)
